Shared drifted-anchor extraction contract in which git span history's current section builds each live snapshot from stale_output's raw location bytes — read at the resolver's healed location for the bytes-equal relocation statuses stale prints 'moved to' for, and back at the declared address for every other status, with absence preserved through the Option-carrying byte read so a missing file is never conflated with an empty one — and applies the commit path's policy on both axes: strict-decoding the bytes so a non-UTF-8 live side classifies as structurally unavailable exactly like the commit path, and slicing the declared range through git.rs's single slice_line_range so a range with no overlap past end-of-file classifies as range-past-eof instead of fabricating an empty text side, with the resolver's nothing-resolves arm re-asking the declared address so 'nothing resolved' and 'no such file' stay different facts.
